※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4544

※ Nothing crosses from one unit to another in a single step, because a step
※ that did would be the mistake units exist to catch written in one place
※ instead of none.  A value that has a unit reaches another through `⎕drop` and
※ then `⎕unit`, which is two things said out loud.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let n: u32 ¤meter = 5
    let m: u32 ¤second = ⎕unit(n, ⌜second⌝)
    0u6
